<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thérouanne</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tarvenna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thérouanne is a village in the Pas-de-Calais in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, on the site of Tarvenna, the Roman capital of the Morini. It became the seat of a large bishopric in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and grew into a fortified town on the border between France and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. In 1553 Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> captured it and razed it to the ground, and its diocese was divided.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/therouanne.jpg" alt="Thérouanne" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Friedrich Tellberg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Th%C3%A9rouanneVillage.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
